{"id": "EUVD-2026-96372", "enisaUuid": "129b4221-e50d-3615-b1ab-c3adcbfdbc33", "description": "argocd-mcp (Argo CD MCP Server) through 0.9.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the delete_application tool that allows MCP clients to reach unintended API endpoints via unvalidated applicationName values. Attackers or prompt-injected models can supply dot-segment values like ../repositories/ to send authenticated DELETE requests deleting repositories, clusters, or projects within the token's RBAC permissions.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T16:14:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:03:13", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/argocd-mcp-delete-application-route-smuggling", "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/mcp-for-argocd/blob/28d15ca69b0c31387cc6ec73d201fd13c5d22b6a/src/argocd/client.ts#L115-L139", "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/mcp-for-argocd/blob/28d15ca69b0c31387cc6ec73d201fd13c5d22b6a/src/argocd/http.ts#L86-L91", "https://github.com/argoproj-labs/mcp-for-argocd", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/argocd-mcp-through-0.9.0-path-traversal-via-delete-application-tool"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f7cg-qc77-hh95", "CVE-2026-108585"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.29, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6f5e6e2e-fe7b-3c1a-8a65-9b19bfc8c469", "product": {"name": "argocd-mcp", "vendor": {"name": "argoproj-labs"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b80de717-ab23-3f88-b2bb-7cd1c81aab4b", "vendor": {"name": "argoproj-labs"}}], "isExploited": false}